From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8953: add the APSS watchdog, disabled

MSM8953 has the APSS watchdog at the same address as its siblings
MSM8937 and MSM8917, whose device trees already describe it with the
QCS404 compatible. Add the node, disabled: whether this SoC's firmware
lets Linux run it is to be checked on a device, one boot at a time,
before any board enables it.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953.dtsi | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953.dtsi
@@ -2899,6 +2899,13 @@
 			#interconnect-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		watchdog@b017000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,apss-wdt-qcs404", "qcom,kpss-wdt";
+			reg = <0x0b017000 0x1000>;
+			clocks = <&sleep_clk>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		cpr: power-controller@b018000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,msm8953-cpr4pd";
 
